\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces A sketch of the considered system. The vector $\mathbf  {m}|_0$ denotes the magnetic moment at $t=0$. One can see that the angle between $\mathbf  {m}$ and $\mathbf  {B}$ at any point in time is the difference between $\beta $ and $\theta $. Since $\cos $ is symmetric on $\mathbb  {R}$, the change of sign as $\mathbf  {m}$ passes $\mathbf  {B}$ is not of concern.}}{25}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
